  // WHAT THE HOUSE REMEMBERS - ballad.
  //
  // The whole song is one long crescendo, which is what a ballad is: it opens
  // on piano alone at an intensity of 0.15 and finishes at 0.92 with the full
  // band. Nothing else in the presets asks the arrangement to build over six
  // minutes' worth of sections rather than eight bars.
  //
  // The instruments arrive one at a time and none of them leaves once it is
  // in: piano, then bass, then drums, then guitar. The order is the structure.
  //
  // Triads throughout - a ballad in power chords is a ballad with the tune
  // taken out - which comes free from the style not being a heavy one.

